ving lived aboard a sailboat for 10 years, completing the US Coast Guard Captain training & sailed the Eastern Pacific coastline from San Francisco, California to Ecuador & the Galapagos Islands. <\/p>","color_text":"#ffffff","color_background":"#171717"}},"profile_GkeiMW":{"type":"profile","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/MT_AG1_Dinner.jpg","heading":"Chef Miriam","text":"<p>Miriam is a certified Functional Nutrition Coach and Private Chef whose healing journey deepened her belief in food as medicine and shaped her focus on autoimmune conditions. Now rooted in Ojai’s agricultural valley, she works with organizations in the regenerative movement, weaving storytelling, experiential learning, and education to inspire systems-level awareness. She believes some of the most profound learning happens over a meal—at home, with food grown nearby, and a community that honors your seat at the table.<\/p>","color_text":"#ffffff","color_background":"#171717"}},"profile_6VdAqa":{"type":"profile","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Screenshot_2025-05-24_at_9.23.35_AM.png","heading":"Chef Clark","text":"<p>Clark worked at Chef Dan Barber’s two Michelin star restaurant, Blue Hill at Stone Barn, in New York as a line cook for two years. He’s worked fall harvest at Morning Glory Farm in Edgartown, Massachusetts, and as a Venture Fellow at Food Future Co. in New York. He holds a BA in philosophy and economics from Claremont McKenna College.<br\/><\/p>","color_text":"#ffffff","color_background":"#171717"}},"profile_KdtE34":{"type":"profile","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Screenshot_2025-07-03_at_8.20.57_AM.png","heading":"Chef Nico","text":"<p>Nicolas Torrent, founder of Circadian Research, brings over a decade of experience as a private chef for high-performance individuals and wellness-focused families. His approach to food is rooted in functional medicine, circadian rhythm alignment, and ancestral wisdom. Chef Nico is currently available for hir